30,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It seems a large upfront commitment is a barrier for new people, and calculating partial fees is a manual hassle.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. The administrative cost of collecting small, frequent payments is staggering compared to a single annual collection.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings show a stark imbalance. A tiny group does all the work and attends everything, while many others barely appear.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,I've found that charging per event kills the habit of attending. People stop feeling like they belong when every visit has a price tag.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Most of our costs are fixed—hall hire and insurance. We pay those regardless of who shows up. We can't rely on ""pay-as-you-go.""","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, if a few people are doing everything, a flat fee might feel unfair to those who rarely attend.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While true, @Asuka, the treasurer's sanity is at stake. Chasing individual payments is a recipe for burnout.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. The burden of labor is as uneven as the attendance. Those who contribute most are already carrying the club.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"But if we make it too tiered or complex, we risk that ""hesitancy"" I mentioned. People should just show up.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,We also have people struggling to pay the full amount at once. The bank statements show we need flexibility.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we want to keep the ""drift in"" culture, we can't have a rigid, high-entry barrier.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Logic suggests a balance. We need the efficiency of annual collection but perhaps a way to accommodate different levels of use.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I worry that a flat fee continues to subsidize those who never show up, which is causing resentment among the regulars.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"And I worry that any ""per-event"" charge will turn our club into a series of transactions rather than a community.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"We can't afford to be purely ""community-driven"" if we can't cover the hall hire. The fixed costs are the priority.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
