60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option C is out; it scares off newcomers and kills attendance. Option B might be too visible and create social friction.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option C is an administrative nightmare for the treasurer. Option A is the most efficient, though perhaps the least flexible.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option A feels unfair given the attendance gap. Option B acknowledges the different levels of use, which might soothe the regulars.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option B sounds like it creates ""grades"" of members. That's exactly the kind of thing that makes people hesitate to join in.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option A is the only way to ensure our fixed costs are covered without guesswork. We know the money is there.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, but what about the people who can't pay all at once? Option A is a high barrier.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,We can allow payment plans for Option A without changing the structure itself. It keeps the bookkeeping simple.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,I still lean toward B. It's more honest about how the club is actually used.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, honesty is good, but so is a welcoming atmosphere. A flat fee means everyone is an equal member.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"Exactly. And it stops us from having to do ""hand-worked calculations"" for every single person who joins mid-year.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we go with A, we must ensure it's a reasonable amount that doesn't deter the ""taster"" crowd.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed. The simplicity of A outweighs the perceived fairness of B or the flexibility of C.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I suppose if the alternative is the chaos of C, A is a safer harbor for the club's peace.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm convinced. A flat fee removes the mental hurdle of ""should I go tonight?""","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,It's the only way to be sure we aren't running on empty. I'm voting for A.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"I will support A, provided we keep the entry process welcoming.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,A is the only rational choice for the treasurer's longevity.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I'll go with A for the sake of stability, though I remain concerned about the workload balance.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,A it is. Let's make it easy for people to just be part of the club.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"Finally, a decision based on the actual costs.","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
